usage: sample_flux2.py [-h]
                       [--method {full,sca,sca_uniform,sca_layer,sca_switch}]
                       [--label LABEL] [--pi-table PI_TABLE]
                       [--pi-scale PI_SCALE] [--pi-const PI_CONST]
                       [--sigma-star SIGMA_STAR] [--res HxW] --prompts PROMPTS
                       [--start START] [--end END] [--seed SEED]
                       [--steps STEPS] [--guidance GUIDANCE] [--out OUT]
                       [--mu-mode {native,default}] [--n0 N0] [--tile TILE]
                       [--window WINDOW] [--pool {center,mean}]
                       [--gate-sigma GATE_SIGMA] [--route ROUTE]
                       [--chunk CHUNK] [--local-impl {flex,gather}]
                       [--encode-only] [--embedding-cache EMBEDDING_CACHE]
                       [--device DEVICE]

Generate one resumable FLUX.2-dev chunk with full attention or SCA. Output
(PNG + JSON sidecar per prompt, deterministic per-prompt seeds) has the same
format as scripts/sample.py, so the eval scripts run unchanged on --out.
Memory: the Mistral text encoder (~45 GB) and the transformer (~64 GB) do not
fit together on a 96 GB GH200. Prompt embeddings are computed first (cached on
scratch, see sca/flux2.py), the text encoder is freed, then the transformer is
loaded. --encode-only fills the cache and exits.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --method {full,sca,sca_uniform,sca_layer,sca_switch}
  --label LABEL         Method name written to the sidecar (default --method)
  --pi-table PI_TABLE   npz from scripts/calibrate_flux2.py (sca variants)
  --pi-scale PI_SCALE   Calibrated scale to use (default: nearest to target
                        scale)
  --pi-const PI_CONST   Constant pi for every head and sigma (ablation)
  --sigma-star SIGMA_STAR
                        Switch point for sca_switch (default: fitted value)
  --res HxW
  --prompts PROMPTS
  --start START
  --end END
  --seed SEED
  --steps STEPS
  --guidance GUIDANCE   FLUX.2-dev embedded guidance (pipeline default 4)
  --out OUT
  --mu-mode {native,default}
                        native: mu of the 1024^2 sequence length at every
                        resolution (FLUX.1 max_shift analogue); default: the
                        pipeline's linear extrapolation (mu 11.5 at 4096^2)
  --n0 N0
  --tile TILE
  --window WINDOW
  --pool {center,mean}
  --gate-sigma GATE_SIGMA
                        Global-only (pi=0) above this sigma
  --route ROUTE         Hard per-head routing threshold on pi (0 = soft mix)
  --chunk CHUNK         Query tiles per local-branch chunk, gather only
  --local-impl {flex,gather}
  --encode-only         Fill the prompt-embedding cache and exit
  --embedding-cache EMBEDDING_CACHE
                        Prompt-embedding cache directory; default preserves
                        the campaign cache
  --device DEVICE
